", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. The worker has recovered, but payments-api still has a high error rate.\n\n**Rollback:** payments-worker went from v3.4.0 back to v3.4.0's predecessor, v3.3.0, its last version that was healthy in production. It's now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. A human approver signed off before it went out. The worker reports healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** INC-0001 (\"payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy\") is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. My first attempt to create it timed out. I checked the incident list, saw it hadn't been created, and retried with the same idempotency key, so there's only one incident and one page.\n\n**Still a problem:** right after the rollback, payments-api (v5.1.0) was still unhealthy with an 18% error rate. It may just need time to recover, for example while retries or queued work clear. If it stays high, the worker may not be the only cause, and payments-api's own v5.1.0 deploy should be checked. Its last healthy version is v5.0.0. I haven't changed payments-api. Let me know if you want me to keep checking it or roll it back too.", "type": "text"}]}]}